1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,484
Welcome to Unit Six of Algebra Two:
rational expressions and functions. We

2
00:00:05,484 --> 00:00:07,040
start by simplifying.

3
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:12,839
A rational expression is a fraction whose
top and bottom are polynomials.

4
00:00:13,289 --> 00:00:18,302
For example, x squared minus nine, over x
squared plus x minus six.

5
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:23,764
The denominator can't be zero, so some x
values are excluded.

6
00:00:24,214 --> 00:00:30,883
x squared plus x minus six is x plus three
times x minus two. So x can't be negative

7
00:00:30,883 --> 00:00:31,915
three or two.

8
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:37,449
To simplify, factor the top and bottom,
then cancel common factors.

9
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:44,161
The top is x plus three times x minus
three. Cancel x plus three, and you get x

10
00:00:44,161 --> 00:00:48,203
minus three, over x minus two. The
exclusions stay.

11
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:54,347
Watch for opposites. Two minus x is
negative one times x minus two.

12
00:00:54,797 --> 00:00:59,405
So x minus two, over two minus x,
simplifies to negative one.

13
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:02,773
Only cancel factors, never terms.

14
00:01:03,223 --> 00:01:09,186
In x plus five over five, you can't cancel
the fives, because five is added on top,

15
00:01:09,186 --> 00:01:10,263
not multiplied.

16
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,712
Your turn. Simplify x squared minus four
x, over x squared minus sixteen.

17
00:01:17,162 --> 00:01:18,698
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:19,148 --> 00:01:25,722
The top is x times x minus four, and the
bottom is x plus four times x minus four.

19
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:32,055
So the answer is x over x plus four, with
x not equal to four or negative four.

20
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:38,017
Multiplying and dividing rational
expressions works like fractions, with

21
00:01:38,017 --> 00:01:39,088
factoring first.

22
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:45,908
To multiply, factor everything, cancel
common factors, then multiply what's left.

23
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:53,884
Multiply x squared minus one over x plus
two, times three x plus six over x minus

24
00:01:53,884 --> 00:01:54,223
one.

25
00:01:54,673 --> 00:02:01,803
Factor: x plus one times x minus one over
x plus two, times three times x plus two

26
00:02:01,803 --> 00:02:09,194
over x minus one. Cancel x minus one and x
plus two. The answer is three times x plus

27
00:02:09,194 --> 00:02:09,542
one.

28
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:14,805
To divide, multiply by the reciprocal of
the second expression.

29
00:02:15,255 --> 00:02:16,471
Keep, change, flip.

30
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:23,403
Divide x squared minus nine over two x, by
x plus three over four x squared.

31
00:02:23,853 --> 00:02:30,042
Flip and multiply: x plus three times x
minus three over two x, times four x

32
00:02:30,042 --> 00:02:35,906
squared over x plus three. That simplifies
to two x times x minus three.

33
00:02:37,033 --> 00:02:41,428
Exclusions come from every denominator,
including the one you flipped.

34
00:02:41,878 --> 00:02:44,459
Here x can't be zero or negative three.

35
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:51,709
Your turn. Multiply x over x plus five,
times x squared minus twenty-five over x

36
00:02:51,709 --> 00:02:52,320
squared.

37
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:54,306
Pause the video and try it.

38
00:02:54,756 --> 00:02:57,252
Cancel to get x minus five over x.

39
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:03,392
Adding rational expressions needs a common
denominator, just like fractions.

40
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:07,413
With the same denominator, add the
numerators.

41
00:03:07,863 --> 00:03:11,085
Three over x plus five over x is eight
over x.

42
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:17,080
Otherwise, find the least common
denominator: every factor, each to its

43
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,036
highest power.

44
00:03:18,486 --> 00:03:25,163
For one over x squared and one over x
times x plus one, the LCD is x squared

45
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:26,657
times x plus one.

46
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,576
Add two over x plus one, and three over x
minus two.

47
00:03:32,026 --> 00:03:39,590
The LCD is x plus one times x minus two.
Rewrite: two times x minus two, plus three

48
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:42,415
times x plus one, over the LCD.

49
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:50,243
The top is five x minus one. So the sum is
five x minus one, over x plus one times x

50
00:03:50,243 --> 00:03:51,121
minus two.

51
00:03:52,267 --> 00:03:56,768
When subtracting, the minus sign applies
to the whole second numerator.

52
00:03:57,218 --> 00:04:04,043
x over x minus three, minus three over x
minus three, is x minus three over x minus

53
00:04:04,043 --> 00:04:05,687
three, which is one.

54
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:09,735
Always factor the result and cancel if you
can.

55
00:04:10,867 --> 00:04:14,621
Your turn. Add one over x, plus two over x
plus one.

56
00:04:15,071 --> 00:04:16,607
Pause the video and try it.

57
00:04:17,057 --> 00:04:24,096
The LCD is x times x plus one. The top is
x plus one plus two x, so the answer is

58
00:04:24,096 --> 00:04:27,745
three x plus one, over x times x plus one.

59
00:04:28,866 --> 00:04:32,813
In this lesson, we'll solve equations with
rational expressions.

60
00:04:33,933 --> 00:04:39,225
Multiply both sides by the LCD. That
clears every fraction, leaving a

61
00:04:39,225 --> 00:04:40,759
polynomial equation.

62
00:04:41,899 --> 00:04:45,355
Solve x over three plus x over four equals
seven.

63
00:04:45,805 --> 00:04:52,056
Multiply by twelve: four x plus three x
equals eighty-four. So x equals twelve.

64
00:04:53,199 --> 00:04:58,533
Solve x over x minus three equals three
over x minus three, plus two.

65
00:04:58,983 --> 00:05:05,814
Multiply by x minus three: x equals three
plus two times x minus three, which is two

66
00:05:05,814 --> 00:05:08,497
x minus three. So x equals three.

67
00:05:08,947 --> 00:05:14,912
But x equals three makes the denominator
zero. It's an extraneous solution, so this

68
00:05:14,912 --> 00:05:17,715
equation has no solution. Always check.

69
00:05:18,833 --> 00:05:22,182
When each side is a single fraction,
cross-multiply.

70
00:05:22,632 --> 00:05:29,421
Three over x plus one equals two over x.
So three x equals two x plus two, and x

71
00:05:29,421 --> 00:05:30,355
equals two.

72
00:05:31,499 --> 00:05:37,482
Work problems use rates. One pipe fills a
tank in three hours, another in six.

73
00:05:37,482 --> 00:05:41,547
Together: one third plus one sixth equals
one over t.

74
00:05:41,997 --> 00:05:47,821
Multiply by six t: two t plus t equals
six. So t equals two hours.

75
00:05:48,966 --> 00:05:53,275
Your turn. Solve five over x equals three
over x minus two.

76
00:05:53,725 --> 00:05:55,261
Pause the video and try it.

77
00:05:55,711 --> 00:06:02,230
Cross-multiply: five x minus ten equals
three x. So x equals five. Check: neither

78
00:06:02,230 --> 00:06:03,839
denominator is zero.

79
00:06:04,966 --> 00:06:10,024
Rational functions have graphs that
approach lines called asymptotes. In this

80
00:06:10,024 --> 00:06:11,601
lesson, we'll find them.

81
00:06:12,733 --> 00:06:18,796
The parent y equals one over x has two
branches. It approaches the x axis and the

82
00:06:18,796 --> 00:06:20,967
y axis without touching them.

83
00:06:21,417 --> 00:06:23,295
Those axes are its asymptotes.

84
00:06:24,433 --> 00:06:29,083
A vertical asymptote occurs where the
simplified denominator is zero.

85
00:06:29,533 --> 00:06:34,547
For f of x equals two x over x minus
three, it's x equals three.

86
00:06:35,666 --> 00:06:41,224
For the horizontal asymptote, compare
degrees. If the bottom degree is bigger,

87
00:06:41,224 --> 00:06:42,578
it's y equals zero.

88
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:48,976
If the degrees are equal, it's the ratio
of leading coefficients. For two x over x

89
00:06:48,976 --> 00:06:51,369
minus three, that's y equals two.

90
00:06:52,499 --> 00:06:59,021
Sketch f of x equals two x over x minus
three. Draw the dashed lines x equals

91
00:06:59,021 --> 00:07:00,969
three and y equals two.

92
00:07:01,419 --> 00:07:05,913
Plot a few points on each side, then draw
the two branches approaching the

93
00:07:05,913 --> 00:07:06,581
asymptotes.

94
00:07:07,699 --> 00:07:14,201
The x intercept is where the top is zero:
x equals zero. The y intercept is f of

95
00:07:14,201 --> 00:07:16,233
zero, which is also zero.

96
00:07:16,683 --> 00:07:18,837
So the graph passes through the origin.

97
00:07:18,966 --> 00:07:26,025
Your turn. Find the asymptotes of f of x
equals three over x plus one, plus two.

98
00:07:26,475 --> 00:07:28,011
Pause the video and try it.

99
00:07:28,461 --> 00:07:33,069
Vertical: x equals negative one.
Horizontal: y equals two.

100
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:39,752
In this last lesson of Unit Six, we'll
handle two special features of rational

101
00:07:39,752 --> 00:07:42,243
graphs: holes and slant asymptotes.

102
00:07:43,367 --> 00:07:48,316
If a factor cancels from the top and
bottom, the graph has a hole there instead

103
00:07:48,316 --> 00:07:49,319
of an asymptote.

104
00:07:49,769 --> 00:07:56,242
x squared minus four over x minus two
simplifies to x plus two, with x not equal

105
00:07:56,242 --> 00:07:56,809
to two.

106
00:07:57,933 --> 00:08:02,115
To find the hole, plug the excluded x into
the simplified form.

107
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:08,559
x plus two at x equals two is four. So
there's an open circle at two comma four.

108
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:14,244
When the top's degree is exactly one more
than the bottom's, there's a slant

109
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:14,841
asymptote.

110
00:08:15,291 --> 00:08:20,433
For x squared plus one over x, the graph
approaches the line y equals x.

111
00:08:21,567 --> 00:08:26,196
Find it by dividing. Take x squared plus
three, over x minus one.

112
00:08:26,646 --> 00:08:32,623
Long division gives x plus one, with
remainder four. So the slant asymptote is

113
00:08:32,623 --> 00:08:34,155
y equals x plus one.

114
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:40,895
The checklist: factor and cancel to find
holes. The remaining zeros of the bottom

115
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:42,553
are vertical asymptotes.

116
00:08:43,003 --> 00:08:48,551
Compare degrees for horizontal or slant
asymptotes. Then find intercepts and

117
00:08:48,551 --> 00:08:49,062
sketch.

118
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:56,626
Your turn. Find the hole of f of x equals
x squared minus x minus six, over x minus

119
00:08:56,626 --> 00:08:57,091
three.

120
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:59,077
Pause the video and try it.

121
00:08:59,527 --> 00:09:05,031
It simplifies to x plus two, with a hole
at x equals three, y equals five.

122
00:09:06,167 --> 00:09:11,760
That completes Unit Six. Next, we'll study
radical functions in Unit Seven. If this

123
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:16,679
helped, subscribe to School Math,
Explained, and turn on notifications so

124
00:09:16,679 --> 00:09:18,903
you don't miss it. See you there.

